module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Torsion.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.Transform.ShortExact
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.AlgebraizeAffine
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.AffineSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionEpiAffine.Basic

/-!
# The strict transform on a chart is the ring-level one

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes, `b : S' ⟶ S` a second morphism and `E` a
quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on `S'`. The strict transform `Stacks.StrictTransform.sheaf f b E F`
of a module `F` on `X` is the quotient of `pr_X^* F` by the submodule of sections supported on
`pr_{S'}^{-1}(Supp E)` ([Stacks, Tag 080D]).

The *ring-level* strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 053H] is a different-looking construction: the
base change `R[I/a] ⊗_R M` modulo its `a`-power torsion. This file identifies the two on a
chart, that is, on an affine open of `X ×_S S'` on which the inverse image of `E` is generated by
a single section `a` — which is what a blowup chart is, the inverse image of the exceptional ideal
on the chart attached to a section `a` of the centre being generated by the image of `a`
(`Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart`). Over such an open the submodule
divided out is the `a`-power torsion, and the sections of the strict transform are the sections of
`pr_X^* F` modulo that torsion.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.supportedSectionsSubmodule_eq_torsion'`: on an affine open on which a subset
  is the zero locus of a single section `a`, the sections of a quasi-coherent module supported on
  that subset are the submodule of `a`-power torsion.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.exceptionalPreimage_inter_eq_zeroLocus`: on an affine open of the base
  change, `pr_{S'}^{-1}(Supp E)` is the zero locus of the inverse image of `E`.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.supportedSectionsSubmodule_exceptionalPreimage_eq_torsion'`: so on a
  chart the submodule divided out in forming the strict transform is the `a`-power torsion
  submodule — the one the ring-level strict transform divides out.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsCokernelEquivOfAffineOpen`: over an affine open the sections of a
  cokernel of quasi-coherent modules are the sections of the target modulo the range of the
  sections of the map.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsion`: **the comparison.** On a chart the
  sections of the sheaf-level strict transform are the sections of `pr_X^* F` modulo `a`-power
  torsion.

## Implementation notes

The one-element torsion description of the supported sections is
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_supportedSectionsSubmodule_iff_exists_pow_smul_eq_zero`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/Transform/ShortExact.lean`), which was private there and
is
made public rather than copied; what is added here is the passage from its hypothesis — the
complement of the subset inside the affine open is the basic open of `a` — to the zero-locus form
that an ideal sheaf delivers, and the submodule (rather than membership) statement.

The comparison itself is two facts put together. The range of the inclusion of a submodule sheaf
on sections over an open is that submodule, which the torsion description then computes; and over
an affine open the sections of a cokernel are the cokernel of the sections. The second is
`AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsCokernelEquivOfAffineOpen`, assembled here from two statements
about evaluation at an affine open: it preserves epimorphisms of quasi-coherent modules
(`Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_app_of_isAffineOpen`) and it is exact
(`Stacks.Algebraization.affine_sections_cokernel_exact`). `AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsCokernelEquiv`
is the same statement for an affine *scheme* and the open `⊤`, which is not enough here: the base
change along a blowup is not affine, only its charts are.

The hypothesis `QuasiCompact (exceptionalComplement f b E).ι` is what makes the submodule of
supported sections quasi-coherent ([Stacks, Tag 07ZP], via
`Stacks.StrictTransform.isQuasicoherent_supportedSectionsObj`), which the cokernel comparison
needs of both its arguments; for a blowup it holds with no hypothesis ([Stacks, Tag 07ZT],
`Stacks.StrictTransform.quasiCompact_exceptionalComplement_ι`).

The passage from the quotient below to a quotient of a *base change*, which is the shape the
ring-level strict transform has, is
`Stacks.StrictTransform.sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsionBaseChange` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/StrictTransformChartRing.lean`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso`; and the ring-level cancellation turning
such a quotient into `strictTransform I a M` is
`strictTransformEquivBaseChangeQuotientTorsion` in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/StrictTransformBaseChange.lean`. What is *not* in either is the
identification of the base change ring itself: that `Γ(X ×_S S', V)` on a blowup chart is
`R[I/a] ⊗_R Γ(X, U)`. The chart ring identifications
`Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization` and
`Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebra` are the available ingredients for it.

The hypothesis `ha` below is a theorem for a blowup; it is discharged in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/StrictTransformChartBlowUp.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_supportedSectionsSubmodule_iff_exists_pow_smul_eq_zero` in zero-locus
form: a subset meets an affine open in the zero locus of a section `a` exactly when the basic
open of `a` is the part of that open outside the subset. -/
theorem basicOpen_eq_inter_compl_iff_inter_eq_zeroLocus {X : Scheme.{u}} (Z : Set X)
    {U : X.Opens} (a : Γ(X, U)) :
    (X.basicOpen a : Set X) = (U : Set X) ∩ Zᶜ ↔
      Z ∩ (U : Set X) = X.zeroLocus (U := U) ({a} : Set Γ(X, U)) ∩ (U : Set X) := by
  rw [X.zeroLocus_singleton]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩ <;> ext x
  · by_cases hxU : x ∈ (U : Set X)
    · simp only [Set.mem_inter_iff, hxU, and_true, Set.mem_compl_iff]
      exact ⟨fun hxZ hxa ↦ ((h ▸ hxa).2 : x ∉ Z) hxZ, fun hxa ↦ by
        by_contra hxZ
        exact hxa (h ▸ ⟨hxU, hxZ⟩)⟩
    · simp [hxU]
  · refine ⟨fun hxa ↦ ⟨X.basicOpen_le a hxa, fun hxZ ↦ ?_⟩, fun ⟨hxU, hxZ⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
    · exact ((Set.ext_iff.mp h x).mp ⟨hxZ, X.basicOpen_le a hxa⟩).1 hxa
    · by_contra hxa
      exact hxZ ((Set.ext_iff.mp h x).mpr ⟨hxa, hxU⟩).1

/-- **The supported sections cut out by a single section are its powers' torsion.** Over an
affine open on which a subset is the zero locus of a single section `a`, the sections of a
quasi-coherent module supported on that subset form the submodule of `a`-power torsion.

This is the submodule form of
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_supportedSectionsSubmodule_iff_exists_pow_smul_eq_zero`, and it is the
submodule that the ring-level strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 053H] divides out. -/
theorem supportedSectionsSubmodule_eq_torsion' {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (Z : Set X) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (a : Γ(X, U))
    (hZ : Z ∩ (U : Set X) = X.zeroLocus (U := U) ({a} : Set Γ(X, U)) ∩ (U : Set X)) :
    (supportedSectionsSubmodule Z F).toSubmodule.obj (op U) =
      Submodule.torsion' Γ(X, U) Γ(F, U) (Submonoid.powers a) :=
  SetLike.ext fun s ↦
    (mem_supportedSectionsSubmodule_iff_exists_pow_smul_eq_zero F hU a
        ((basicOpen_eq_inter_compl_iff_inter_eq_zeroLocus Z a).mpr hZ) s).trans
      (Iff.trans ⟨fun ⟨n, hn⟩ ↦ ⟨⟨a ^ n, n, rfl⟩, hn⟩, fun ⟨c, hc⟩ ↦ by
        obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := c.2
        exact ⟨n, by rw [show (a : Γ(X, U)) ^ n = (c : Γ(X, U)) from hn]; exact hc⟩⟩
        (Submodule.mem_torsion'_iff _ _).symm)

/-- The range on sections of the inclusion of the supported-sections submodule sheaf is that
submodule. -/
theorem range_sectionsLinearMap_supportedSectionsι {X : Scheme.{u}} (Z : Set X) (F : X.Modules)
    (U : X.Opens) :
    LinearMap.range (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap (supportedSectionsι Z F) U) =
      (supportedSectionsSubmodule Z F).toSubmodule.obj (op U) :=
  Submodule.ext fun s ↦
    ⟨fun ⟨t, ht⟩ ↦ ht ▸ t.2, fun hs ↦ ⟨⟨s, hs⟩, rfl⟩⟩

/-- **Over an affine open the sections of a cokernel of quasi-coherent modules are the sections
of the target modulo the range of the sections of the map.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsCokernelEquiv` over an affine *open* of an arbitrary scheme rather
than over an affine scheme: the quotient map is surjective on sections over an affine open
because evaluation there preserves epimorphisms of quasi-coherent modules
(`Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_app_of_isAffineOpen`), and its kernel is the range because
evaluation there is exact (`Stacks.Algebraization.affine_sections_cokernel_exact`). -/
def sectionsCokernelEquivOfAffineOpen {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules}
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [N.IsQuasicoherent] (φ : M ⟶ N) (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (Γ(N, U.1) ⧸ LinearMap.range (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap φ U.1))
      ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(cokernel φ, U.1) := by
  have hqc : (cokernel φ).IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentColimits.isQuasicoherent_cokernel φ
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective
      (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap (cokernel.π φ) U.1) :=
    Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_app_of_isAffineOpen X (cokernel.π φ) U.1 U.2
  have hex : Function.Exact (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap φ U.1)
      (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap (cokernel.π φ) U.1) :=
    Stacks.Algebraization.affine_sections_cokernel_exact φ U
  rw [← hex.linearMap_ker_eq]
  exact LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective _ hsurj

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Stacks.StrictTransform

variable {X S S' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (b : S' ⟶ S) (E : S'.IdealSheafData)

/-- **On an affine open of the base change, `pr_{S'}^{-1}(Supp E)` is the zero locus of the
inverse image of `E`.** The support of an inverse image ideal sheaf is the preimage of the
support, and on an affine open the support of an ideal sheaf is the zero locus of its ideal
there. -/
theorem exceptionalPreimage_inter_eq_zeroLocus (V : (baseChange f b).affineOpens) :
    exceptionalPreimage f b E ∩ (V.1 : Set (baseChange f b)) =
      (baseChange f b).zeroLocus (U := V.1)
        ((E.comap (pullback.snd f b)).ideal V : Set Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)) ∩
          (V.1 : Set (baseChange f b)) := by
  have h : exceptionalPreimage f b E =
      ((E.comap (pullback.snd f b)).support : Set (baseChange f b)) := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
    rfl
  rw [h]
  exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_inter _ V

/-- On an affine open of the base change on which the inverse image of `E` is generated by a
single section `a`, the subset `pr_{S'}^{-1}(Supp E)` is the zero locus of `a`. For `b` the blowup
of `S` in an ideal sheaf and `E` its exceptional ideal, a blowup chart is such an open. -/
theorem exceptionalPreimage_inter_eq_zeroLocus_singleton (V : (baseChange f b).affineOpens)
    (a : Γ(baseChange f b, V.1))
    (ha : (E.comap (pullback.snd f b)).ideal V = Ideal.span {a}) :
    exceptionalPreimage f b E ∩ (V.1 : Set (baseChange f b)) =
      (baseChange f b).zeroLocus (U := V.1) ({a} : Set Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)) ∩
        (V.1 : Set (baseChange f b)) :=
  (exceptionalPreimage_inter_eq_zeroLocus f b E V).trans
    (by rw [ha, (baseChange f b).zeroLocus_span])

/-- **The submodule divided out in forming the strict transform is the `a`-power torsion on a
chart.** On an affine open `V` of `X ×_S S'` on which the inverse image of `E` is generated by a
single section `a`, the sections over `V` of a quasi-coherent module supported on
`pr_{S'}^{-1}(Supp E)` are exactly the `a`-power torsion.

This is the submodule the ring-level strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 053H] divides out. -/
theorem supportedSectionsSubmodule_exceptionalPreimage_eq_torsion'
    (G : (baseChange f b).Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent]
    (V : (baseChange f b).affineOpens) (a : Γ(baseChange f b, V.1))
    (ha : (E.comap (pullback.snd f b)).ideal V = Ideal.span {a}) :
    (Scheme.Modules.supportedSectionsSubmodule (exceptionalPreimage f b E)
        G).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1) =
      Submodule.torsion' Γ(baseChange f b, V.1) Γ(G, V.1) (Submonoid.powers a) :=
  supportedSectionsSubmodule_eq_torsion' _ G V.2 a
    (exceptionalPreimage_inter_eq_zeroLocus_singleton f b E V a ha)

/-- **The sheaf-level strict transform is the ring-level one on a chart.** Suppose the base
change `X ×_S S'` carries an affine open `V` on which the inverse image of `E` is generated by a
single section `a` — which is the situation on a blowup chart, the inverse image of the
exceptional ideal there being generated by the image of the section the chart is attached to.
Then the sections over `V` of the strict transform of a quasi-coherent module `F` are the
sections of `pr_X^* F` over `V` modulo their `a`-power torsion.

That quotient is precisely the ring-level strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 053H]: by
`AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso` the sections of `pr_X^* F` over `V` are
the base change `Γ(X ×_S S', V) ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(F, U)` of the sections of `F` along `pr_X`, and
`strictTransform I a M` is such a base change modulo its `a`-power torsion. -/
def sectionsSheafEquivQuotientTorsion (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [QuasiCompact (exceptionalComplement f b E).ι]
    (V : (baseChange f b).affineOpens) (a : Γ(baseChange f b, V.1))
    (ha : (E.comap (pullback.snd f b)).ideal V = Ideal.span {a}) :
    (Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst f b)).obj F, V.1) ⧸
          Submodule.torsion' Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)
            Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst f b)).obj F, V.1)
            (Submonoid.powers a))
        ≃ₗ[Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)] Γ(sheaf f b E F, V.1) := by
  have hrange : LinearMap.range (Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap
        (Scheme.Modules.supportedSectionsι (exceptionalPreimage f b E)
          ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst f b)).obj F)) V.1) =
      Submodule.torsion' Γ(baseChange f b, V.1)
        Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst f b)).obj F, V.1)
        (Submonoid.powers a) :=
    (range_sectionsLinearMap_supportedSectionsι _ _ _).trans
      (supportedSectionsSubmodule_exceptionalPreimage_eq_torsion' f b E _ V a ha)
  rw [← hrange]
  exact sectionsCokernelEquivOfAffineOpen _ V

end Stacks.StrictTransform

end
